# GOLDEN-COVERAGE RA NOT_PROVEN
# GROUND-TRUTH: kill case K9, and the most dangerous of the set — BIN
#   COVERAGE is the one proven tier with NO post-hoc net (the sampling gate
#   does not run on bins; SOUNDNESS_PROOF s8 item 3), so nothing else stood
#   between this claim and a user.
#
#   `bins BTag(jets[0]) 0 1 2` gives bins [0,1) [1,2) [2,inf), with everything
#   below 0 falling OUTSIDE every bin. Coverage asks whether every event In RA
#   lands in SOME bin. Until 2026-08-01 the answer was "proven": TAG said
#   btag in {0,1}, which entails btag >= 0, which fills the underflow.
#
#   It is FALSE. An event with one btag-less jet is In RA (`size(jets) >= 1`)
#   and lands in NO bin -- `smash2 run` reports `bin=underflow` for it.
#   Under the presence model the coverage query keeps the `defined` variable
#   free and the gap witness NAMES it:
#     coverage: not proven (gap witness: defined(jets[0].btag) = 0,
#                           jets[0].btag = -1, size(jets) = 1)
#   which is not just prevention but a readable explanation.
#
#   This pin must stay NOT_PROVEN. If it ever flips to PROVEN, a fact
#   somewhere is claiming an absent property has a value.

object jets
  take Jet
  select pt > 30

region RA
  select size(jets) >= 1
  bins BTag(jets[0]) 0 1 2
